From: cloveian
Date: Wed, 15 Apr 2026 17:18:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] sound: soc: intel: sof_sdw: Force SmartAmp/SmartMic DAI names for Surface Pro 11

The sof_sdw DAI link naming logic falls through to a generic name when
append_dai_type is not set, which doesn't match the function topology
filenames expected by SOF for Surface Pro 11 (Snapdragon X / Intel
configuration with SoundWire SmartAmp and SmartMic endpoints).

Force "Playback-SmartAmp" / "Capture-SmartMic" names explicitly for
AMP and MIC DAI types when append_dai_type is not set, matching the
existing SmartAmp/SmartMic patterns used in function topology files.

Tested on Surface Pro 11 with kernel 7.0.

Signed-off-by: cloveian
---
 sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_sdw.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_sdw.c b/sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_sdw.c
index XXXXXXX..XXXXXXX 100644
--- a/sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_sdw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_sdw.c
@@ -932,15 +932,26 @@ static int sof_sdw_rtd_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 		}

 		/* create stream name according to first link id */
-		if (ctx->append_dai_type)
+		if (ctx->append_dai_type) {
 			name = devm_kasprintf(dev, GFP_KERNEL,
 					      sdw_stream_name[stream + 2],
 					      ffs(sof_end->link_mask) - 1,
 					      type_strings[sof_end->dai_info->dai_type]);
-		else
+		} else if (sof_end->dai_info->dai_type == SOC_SDW_DAI_TYPE_AMP) {
+			/* Force SmartAmp name for amplifiers to match topology expectations */
+			name = devm_kasprintf(dev, GFP_KERNEL, "%s-%s",
+					      stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK ? "Playback" : "Capture",
+					      type_strings[SOC_SDW_DAI_TYPE_AMP]);
+		} else if (sof_end->dai_info->dai_type == SOC_SDW_DAI_TYPE_MIC) {
+			/* Force SmartMic name for mic to match function topology expectations */
+			name = devm_kasprintf(dev, GFP_KERNEL, "%s-%s",
+					      stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK ? "Playback" : "Capture",
+					      type_strings[SOC_SDW_DAI_TYPE_MIC]);
+		} else {
 			name = devm_kasprintf(dev, GFP_KERNEL,
 					      sdw_stream_name[stream],
 					      ffs(sof_end->link_mask) - 1);
+		}
 		if (!name)
 			return -ENOMEM;
